% Comparisons are filters over values of three distinct types.  Integers
% order numerically, symbols and strings bytewise; values of different types
% are never equal, and an ordering between them filters the binding out.
v(-9223372036854775808).
v(-1).
v(9).
v(10).
v(apple).
v(banana).
v("apple").
v("b").

v(X), X < 9?
v(X), X >= apple?
v(X), X > "a"?
v(X), X = apple?
v(X), X != apple, X != "apple", X != "b", X > -1?

% A comparison written before the literal that binds its operand.
N >= 10, v(N)?
